A learner's project contains this grading routine. Marks must be whole numbers from 0 to 100.

```python
def grade(mark_text):
    if not mark_text.isdigit():
        return "Invalid"
    mark = int(mark_text)
    if mark > 100:
        return "Invalid"
    if mark >= 70:
        return "A"
    if mark >= 50:
        return "B"
    return "U"


for item in ["85", "70", "69", "50", "49", "0", "100", "101", "x7"]:
    print(item, grade(item))
```

The method `isdigit()` is true only when the text is made up only of digits.
